## POSITION TYPE
**Type A** — Single-driver thesis. Eos's investment case rests on one primary mechanism: domestic non-lithium battery manufacturing capturing grid-scale storage demand via 45X PTC economics and FIAC-driven competitive displacement. There is one manufacturing location, one product (Z3 cube), one regulatory environment (U.S. federal energy policy), and one primary distribution channel (direct to developers/utilities). International MOUs (U.K., Asia Pacific) are early-stage and not yet revenue-contributing. Data center demand is an emerging sub-segment within the same product/channel structure, not an independent driver.

**Fixed cap: 35%** with graduated exit ratchet.

