## FRESH MONEY TEST
**Fresh money allocation: 4%**

The gap between 4% (fresh money) and 8% (recommended maximum) reflects the following: an existing holder has already absorbed the volatility and dilution of this company's history and is positioned for the thesis to play out; a fresh buyer today is entering at a point where the H2 revenue bridge is the single most important near-term catalyst, and that bridge has not yet been demonstrated. The stock is up 35% as of June 30 (per the mark-to-market disclosure), meaning the market has already partially priced in the positive BBB outcome and manufacturing progress. A fresh buyer is paying for execution that has not yet occurred. The 4% fresh allocation reflects genuine conviction in the thesis with appropriate caution about entry timing and execution risk on the H2 ramp.

